    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="1090" n="976" xml:id="pg976"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.602 Ot 81/213: telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Office of Naval Intelligence, Navy Department, to
                        the Naval Station at Constantinople</hi><anchor n="45" xml:id="d864-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">2 October,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>1602. Your 0031–1800. Following sent with approval General Goethals. Referring
                    cablegram September eleventh to Goethals and Barnard, Major Kennedy has no
                    authority to act on Chester Project. He is proceeding under false pretense and
                    is repudiated by Goethals and all other purported stockholders found.</p>
                <p>It is believed Abdul Hamid heirs’ claim is wildcat scheme concocted in England to
                    antagonize American claim.</p>
                <p>Ottoman Company will be organized on legal basis and Arthur Chester only
                    authorized to represent it in Turkey. Tell Chester have nothing to do with
                    Kennedy. Signed Chester. 1535.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d864-f1" n="45" type="source" xml:id="d864-f1-content">
                <p>Copy received in the Department of State as enclosure to letter of Oct. 10, from
                    the Navy Department.</p>
            </note>
